{
  "about": "QuickFlow.place on both phones: where the copy of a shape at source (x, y, w, h: its unturned frame, turned rotation degrees about its centre when given) goes, side of it (top, right, bottom or left). It is the source's frame size, with a gap of max(40, half the source's side along that way) between them; the copy keeps the source's turn. While it overlaps one of obstacles (their turned boxes, sharing area; touching edges do not count) it moves on that way by its own size, up to 3 times, and stays where it got to. Then it is kept inside bounds (the page): pushed back in on each axis, its left or top on the bounds' when it is the wider. bounds is null on a whiteboard, which grows to take the copy, so nothing pushes it back. box is the result.",
